=== Grondstoffen <sec:grondstoffen-buildings>

2022 global status report for buildings and construction

The Global Status Report for Buildings and Construction (Buildings-GSR) is a flagship publication of the UNEP-hosted Global Alliance for Buildings and Construction (GlobalABC). The Buildings-GSR provides an annual snapshot of the progress of the buildings and construction sector on a global scale and reviews the status of policies, finance, technologies, and solutions to monitor whether the sector is aligned with the Paris Agreement goals. It also provides stakeholders with evidence to persuade policymakers and the overall buildings and construction community to take action.
international energy agency

The IEA works with governments and industry to shape a secure and sustainable energy future for all. On their website, you can read all about questions like: "Why are buildings important?", "Why do buildings matter for clean energy transitions?" and "Where do we need to go?". 

=== Context <sec:context-buildings>

De constructie sector gebruikt 40% van energie en 36% van broeikasgasuitstoot. Het speelt een belangrijke rol in klimaatsverandering, maar het heeft ook lokale effect, meestal zijn steden veel warmer dan hun omgeving. Dit neomt de Heat-island effect en gebeurt door meer absorbatie van zonlicht door gebouwen en infrastructuur zoals wegen. 


